          "ruleId": "DS121708",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Problematic C function detected (memcpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because it is marked as a high-confidence undefined behavior risk due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The analysis detected that the destination and source may refer to overlapping memory areas, which can cause undefined behavior in C/C++ when using functions like memcpy. There are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent this overlap, and the source and destination are derived from dataflow analysis, indicating a real risk. Additionally, the source may be null, which further increases the risk of undefined behavior. No evidence was found to suggest that the destination is a pointer-based member or that the count is derived from the destination's capacity, so the risk remains high.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior caused by overlapping memory regions in memory copy operations, ensure that the source and destination do not overlap. If overlap is possible, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`, as `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. For the given code, replace the memory copy function as follows:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4);\n```\n\nThis change ensures that even if the source and destination regions overlap, the operation will be performed safely without causing undefined behavior. For more information, see the [OWASP C++ Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices/) and [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html).\n\n___\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "rocm_smi/src/rocm_smi_binary_parser.cc"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 140,
                  "startColumn": 4,
                  "endLine": 140,
                  "endColumn": 44,
                  "charOffset": 4406,
                  "charLength": 40,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "memcpy(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4)",
                    "rendered": {
                      "text": "memcpy(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4)",
                      "markdown": "`memcpy(&pmmetrics_version, &buf1[12], 4)`"
                    }
                  },
                  "sourceLanguage": "cpp"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "There are a number of conditions in which memcpy can introduce a vulnerability (mismatched buffer sizes, null pointers, etc.). More secure alternitives perform additional validation of the source and destination buffer"
              },
