          "ruleId": "DS111237",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the code copies a string into a destination buffer using a length parameter whose relationship to the actual buffer size is not proven. The destination buffer is a pointer, and there is no evidence that the length argument is derived from the buffer's actual capacity. Additionally, there is no explicit null-termination after the copy, which can lead to unterminated strings if the source is longer than the specified length. The source is a C-style string, so overlap and null pointer risks are not present, but the main concern is the potential for buffer overflow or string truncation without proper null-termination. This pattern is a common cause of memory safety vulnerabilities in C/C++ code.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate this issue, ensure that the length argument used in the copy operation does not exceed the actual size of the destination buffer. If the destination buffer's size is known, use it directly or compute the minimum of the buffer size and the source string length. Additionally, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer after copying to prevent unterminated strings.\n\nFor example, if you know the size of `name` (e.g., `name` is allocated with `char name[NAME_SIZE];`), you can do:\n\n```cpp\nsize_t name_capacity = NAME_SIZE;\nstrncpy(name, socket->get_socket_id().c_str(), name_capacity - 1);\nname[name_capacity - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\nIf `name` is a pointer and its capacity is not known, ensure that the caller provides the correct buffer size and document this requirement clearly. Always null-terminate the buffer after copying.\n\nFor more information, see:\n- [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n\n___\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/amd_smi/amd_smi.cc"
                },
                "region": {
