          "ruleId": "DS111237",
          "kind": "fail",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
            "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the destination buffer's actual size is not known at compile time, and the code copies up to a maximum length minus one without verifying that the destination buffer is large enough to hold that many bytes. The use of a constant for the copy length does not guarantee that the destination buffer is appropriately sized, which can lead to buffer overflows if the buffer is smaller than expected. There are no explicit checks or guards in the code to ensure the destination buffer's capacity matches or exceeds the copy length. Additionally, there is no explicit null-termination after the copy, which can result in unterminated strings if the source string is longer than the allowed length. The source is a C++ string's c_str(), which is safe from overlap and null pointer issues, but the main risk remains with the destination buffer's unknown size.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo mitigate the risk of buffer overflow, ensure that the destination buffer is at least as large as the maximum copy length. If possible, use safer string copy functions that require the actual size of the destination buffer, or add explicit checks before copying. Additionally, always null-terminate the destination buffer after copying to prevent unterminated strings.\n\nFor example, after the copy operation, explicitly set the last byte to '\\0':\n\n```cpp\nstd::strncpy(market_name, empty.c_str(), AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1);\nmarket_name[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you know the actual size of `market_name`, use `std::snprintf`:\n\n```cpp\nstd::snprintf(market_name, AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH, \"%s\", empty.c_str());\n```\n\nAlways validate that the destination buffer is large enough for the intended operation. For more information, see [OWASP C Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_overflow) and [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html).\n\n___\n"
          },
